msgid "Where is 2.2.0.Final?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Today we announce the availability of Quarkus 2.2.1.Final, which is the "
"result of our first hardening cycle."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Indeed, for 2.2, we decided to slow down on adding new features and focus "
"this release cycle on hardening Quarkus with 3 main focuses:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Fix issues"
msgstr ""

msgid "Improve usability"
msgstr ""

msgid "Improve documentation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Thus the list of noteworthy new features is a bit short for this release:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Upgrade to GraalVM 21.2"
msgstr ""

msgid "Add global flag to disable Dev Services"
msgstr ""

msgid "Change the default thread model for RESTEasy Reactive"
msgstr ""

msgid "Introduce support for MongoDB service binding"
msgstr ""

msgid "Extension for running Narayana LRA participants"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"but overall, this release comes with a lot of nice things so we strongly "
"recommend you to upgrade."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We only released the Core artifacts of 2.2.0.Final and not the full Platform "
"release because this version suffered from a bug preventing dev mode to work "
"on Windows (that's what you get for trying to fix another bug...).\n"
"Thus why we announce 2.2.1.Final directly."
msgstr ""

msgid "Migration Guide"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To migrate from 2.1, please refer to https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"wiki/Migration-Guide-2.2[our migration guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "What&#8217;s new?"
msgstr ""

msgid "GraalVM 21.2"
msgstr ""

msgid "The recommended version of GraalVM to use with Quarkus 2.2 is 21.2."
msgstr ""

msgid "Global flag to disable Dev Services"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is now possible to disable all the Dev Services at once with `quarkus."
"devservices.enabled=false`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Also we centralized all the information about Dev Services in link:/guides/"
"dev-services[one place]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Enhanced thread model for RESTEasy Reactive"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In short, RESTEasy Reactive is now smart enough to choose a blocking or non "
"blocking thread model depending on the prototype of your REST methods,\n"
"which should makes things easier when you are coming from RESTEasy Classic."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Clément Escoffier wrote a very comprehensive blog post about this "
"enhancement that is very much worth reading: https://quarkus.io/blog/"
"resteasy-reactive-smart-dispatch/[RESTEasy Reactive - To block or not to "
"block]."
msgstr ""

msgid "MongoDB service binding"
msgstr ""

msgid "Service bindings got a new component supported: MongoDB."
msgstr ""

msgid "Narayana LRA extension"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"LRA stands for Long Running Actions and the point of it is to provide APIs "
"for services to coordinate activities."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can learn more about it in link:/blog/using-lra[the dedicated blog post]."
""
msgstr ""

msgid "Full Changelog"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can get the full changelogs of https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"releases/tag/2.2.0.CR1[2.2.0.CR1], https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"releases/tag/2.2.0.Final[2.2.0.Final] and https://github.com/quarkusio/"
"quarkus/releases/tag/2.2.1.Final[2.2.1.Final] on GitHub."
msgstr ""

